# The build context of the image.
#
# The image reads six things out of this tree: pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
# README.md, LICENSE, src/ and examples/. Everything else is either
# regenerable or too large to be worth sending to the daemon.
#
# The context used to carry the whole .git directory, and every untracked
# file the working tree happened to hold.
#
# The patterns that name a directory are written "name/*" on purpose: a
# plain "name" would match a directory of that name at any depth, and
# would take a directory inside src/ out of the image. "name/*" only
# matches the one at the root of the context.
#
# The samples are NOT excluded: examples/demo-app/demo.apk is the file the
# image is checked against, and a "*.apk" rule here would take it out of
# the build context and leave the image without a sample to analyse.

# The version control data. Nothing in the image reads it, and it is the
# largest thing in the tree.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# The working area of this machine: the virtual environment, the coverage
# data of a measurement, the analysis output.
.scratch
.venv
venv
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov
junit*.xml
.dexatlas/*
workspace/*
out/*
_decompile/*
jadx-out/*
apktool-out/*

# The caches the tools leave behind.
__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
build/*
dist/*

# The third-party samples the integration suite fetches. They are large,
# they are not the repository's own, and the image does not read them.
fixtures/apk/*

# The editors and the operating systems.
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The documentation and the test suite. The image reads neither.
docs/*
tests/*
benchmarks/*
